268 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 269 0 R/Alt(Panel a is a side view of a long flexible test article held up by three shakers underneath and pushed sideways by a fourth at one end. Four control gauges sit on top of the article, drawn as orange triangles numbered 1 to 4, and a held-out gauge, a green diamond, sits on a component in the middle. Dashed orange arrows carry each control gauge's response up to a box labelled Controller, at every frequency line, once a loop. The box lists its inputs (the reference matrix of target spectra, coherences and phases; the measured response matrix of the control gauges; the frequency response of the setup from a low-level identification), the control law, which works out the next drive matrix, and its output, random drive signals with the drive matrix's spectra and correlations. Solid blue lines carry the drive signals from the controller to each shaker's amplifier. Panel b is a three by three grid for three control gauges. The diagonal cells, blue, hold each gauge's spectrum in g squared per hertz. The cells above the diagonal, orange, hold a coherence and a phase for each pair: 0.8 and 30 degrees, 0.5 and minus 60 degrees, 0.6 and minus 95 degrees. The cells below the diagonal are dashed and read mirror, phase reversed.)/A[<</O/Layout/Placement/Block>>]/K[0]/Pg 953 0 R>>
endobj
