363 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 364 0 R/Alt(A line plot. The horizontal axis is how far the three phases miss closing the loop, theta 1 2 plus theta 2 3 minus theta 1 3, from 0 to 180 degrees. The vertical axis is the smallest eigenvalue of the coherence matrix, from about minus 1.2 to plus 0.5, with the region below zero shaded and labelled as references that cannot be played. Four falling curves: coherence 1.0 on every pair starts at zero and falls to minus 1 at 180 degrees; coherence 0.9, with square markers, starts at 0.05 and crosses zero near 5 degrees; coherence 0.7, with circles, starts at 0.16 and crosses near 20 degrees; coherence 0.5, with triangles, starts at 0.29 and crosses at 45 degrees.)/A[<</O/Layout/Placement/Block>>]/K[0]/Pg 957 0 R>>
endobj
