512 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 513 0 R/Alt(Three panels. Panel a plots, against the number of independent averages from 4 to 1,024 on a log scale, the band containing 90 percent of estimates of one line's spectrum, in dB about the truth, as two solid blue curves, and the 99 percent band as light shading. Dashed lines mark plus and minus 3 dB and dotted lines plus and minus 1 dB. The 90 percent band narrows from about minus 4.6 and plus 2.9 dB at 4 averages to within 1 dB near 60 averages and about 0.2 dB at 1,024. Panel b plots the chance that every line is inside the band against the number of averages per line, for 100 lines (solid, circles), 400 lines (dashed, squares) and 1,600 lines (dotted, triangles), orange for plus or minus 3 dB and pink for plus or minus 1 dB. The 3 dB curves rise from near 0 to near 1 between about 10 and 40 averages; the 1 dB curves rise between about 100 and 400 averages. Panel c plots the phase error not exceeded by 90 percent of estimates, in degrees, against the true coherence of the pair from 0 to 1, for 16, 32, 64 and 128 averages. All curves fall as coherence rises; at coherence 0.5 they read about 17, 12, 8 and 6 degrees. A dashed line marks plus or minus 10 degrees, and the region below coherence 0.5 is shaded as the region where MIL-STD-810H Annex E allows any phase.)/A[<</O/Layout/Placement/Block>>]/K[4]/Pg 963 0 R>>
endobj
